Independent REST memory wire fixtures
====================================

Authority: docs/projects/roadmap/serving-memory-contract.md, especially sections
3-9 and the selected decisions in section 11. No expectations come from Rust or
server output. Run python -B tests\memory_wire_oracle.py --self-test, also with -O.
These are logical/schema goldens, not a running REST adapter qualification.

Each named case has operation, request (method/path/headers/body), independent
view, and expected status/body. A body string denotes raw JSON, allowing duplicate
key and malformed-JSON tests. All other bodies are actual decoded JSON objects.
Errors compare exact status/code/envelope; message text is deliberately ignored:
the contract requires a sanitized string but does not prescribe English wording.
Every rejection declares one defect and a repair; repairing it must make the
exchange acceptable. A repair_check of gate validates authorization and the
repaired capability gate, without inventing a successful unaccepted operation.
A repair_check of structure validates the repaired request only when its
execution mapping is explicitly OPEN. Other repairs must execute successfully.
Every repaired exchange receives an orthogonal unknown-field second defect.

View fields are test injection, not request fields or provisioning APIs:
clock_ms, sequence, tenant (omitted means @root), exact effective scope_grants,
receipt_window_ms (required), next_receipt_id (opaque accessor result), pre_state
(existing agent_memory_oracle fixture steps), receipts (retained logical identity,
request, retry_until_ms and static result), and explicit authorization/capability
or planner observations. Receipt IDs are injected accessor values, not calculated
keys. Semantic request equality is logical only, never a production digest.
No test fabricates a digest encoding or physical-frame byte count.

Input-only compression: {"$text":"x","count":4096}, {"$repeat":object,"count":n,
"enumerate":["id"]}, and {"$properties":typed_scalar,"count":n} expand request/view
inputs. Expected outputs are always literal; they are never expanded, calculated,
sorted, sliced or captured from oracle output.
{"$json_padding":body,"size":n} produces input-only raw JSON plus leading spaces
to test the actual serialized request byte boundary, not a reserialized proxy.

Each family has a literal operation_id and a structural catalog. A structural
case names a schema, input value, request/response direction and valid boolean;
invalid cases declare an expected error and one repair. Special schema values
json, http, exchange and headers exercise decoding and HTTP/envelope rules.
Successful fact/pending structural examples describe only section 8 JSON shapes.

Structural cases exercise the full nine-operation inventory independently of
which core capabilities are accepted. Execution successes are restricted to
accepted core behavior. Unspecified mappings/encodings are recorded as OPEN items
in tests/memory_wire_report.md, not guessed in wire success/error expectations.
Recall views use the ranking reference's id/scope/O/rank/importance vocabulary,
with retained kind/expiry/metadata and optional stored unit vectors. Optional
raw_scores are independently injected eligible-leg BM25/RRF observations, not
computed retrieval expectations. Filters and authoritative scope/kind/owner TTL
are applied independently before ranking. These are not candidate-discovery or
index-analyzer parity claims. Consolidation views use the existing C1 setup
vocabulary; source revisions/expiry are rechecked by that unchanged reference.
